   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Ben<div>This is interesting, it seems worth thinking about in the larger context of methods for measuring mixing.  So I&#39;m ccing Kenny.</div><div>A</div><div><br><div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div>On May 5, 2013, at 12:34 PM, Ben Goodrich wrote:</div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">I was thinking about the distance correlation<br><br><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distance_correlation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distance_correlation&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476665144000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OfjiHoCi2zq6F4S4TA5XX\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distance_correlation</a><br><br>which is a measure of multivariate dependence on [0,1] and is implemented by the energy package for R<br><br><a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/energy/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/energy/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476665144000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3sT2SzGarj6TUSSR3Uf31E\">http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/energy/index.html</a> .<br><br>My thought was to estimate the distance correlation between consecutive MCMC iterations. For each iteration, you can get a &quot;sample&quot; whose rows are equal to the number of chains and whose columns are equal to the number of monitored quantities from the posterior distribution and then calculate the distance correlation to the next &quot;sample&quot;. An R function for doing this is pretty simple:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">dependence </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stanfit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  stopifnot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stanfit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;stanfit&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  stopifnot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stanfit@mode </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  pars </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stanfit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  arr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> extract</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stanfit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> permuted </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inc_warmup </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  arr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> array</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">arr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;chains&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cbind</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,])),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                 dim </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">arr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> pars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">arr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">arr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dcor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),])))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Trying this out on the dogs example<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">stopifnot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rstan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>stopifnot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">energy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan_demo</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;dogs&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>dcors </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dependence</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dcors</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;l&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ylim </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> las </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>     xlab </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Iteration&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ylab </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Distance Correlation&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     main </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit@model_name</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;model&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>lines</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lowess</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dcors</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;l&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>abline</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">v </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>legend</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bottomleft&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> legend </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Value&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Smoothed&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;End Warmup&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>       col </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cex </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>yields the attached plot which shows that this measure of dependence slowly trends downward during the warmup period and levels off at about 0.7 on average.<br><br>What is interesting to me is that (1 - 0.7) * 8000 = 2400, which is in line with the average of the marginal effective sample sizes that we calculate (2247). It is somewhat intuitive that the quantity one minus the average distance correlation times the total number of retained iterations would be a multivariate measure of effective sample size that would be appropriate in the extreme cases where the average distance correlation were 0 or 1. And if you do this on an example like mvn_orange where the defaults yield crappy sampling, the average distance correlation is near 1 and the marginal effective sample sizes are usually in the single digits. But I don&#39;t have much of an idea for a proof that it would be a reasonable multivariate measure of effective sample size for intermediate values of the distance correlations, nor much of an argument that setting the exponent equal to 1.0 is best.<br><br>Ben<br><br><div><br></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
